{
  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the first experiment should establish a strong upper-bound baseline to anchor all subsequent comparisons. config_001 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer aggregation, weighted fusion) combines the most powerful and well-motivated choices across every design axis: multimodal captures complementary RNA+image signal, multiprofile with transformer aggregation is the most expressive way to pool multiple cell profiles, scvi_n200 is the standard learned single-cell RNA representation, ViT-L is the strongest image encoder available, and weighted fusion lets the model learn modality importance. Testing this 'full-power' configuration first tells us the achievable ceiling; if it performs well, later experiments can ablate components (e.g., swap ViT-L→ResNet50, transformer→avgpool, multiprofile→singleprofile) to find cheaper near-equivalent configurations. If it underperforms, we learn early that the architecture needs rethinking. Expected relative cost: HIGH (ViT-L + transformer aggregation + multiprofile + scvi encoder makes this among the most expensive configurations in the search space), but justifiable as the first experiment since establishing the accuracy ceiling is the highest-value information to gain before spending the remaining 9 experiments on targeted ablations."
}

